{"scraped_at": "2026-06-04T07:26:16.694941+00:00", "run_id": "20260604_072616", "page": 30, "api_response": {"count": 3946, "per_page": 20, "current_page": 30, "total_pages": 198, "next": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=31&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "previous": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=29&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "results": [{"review_id": 654891413, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r654891413-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Historical and Religious Place", "text": "One of the most famous  Hindu temple in the world. The history dates back to fifth century AD. This is a Shiva temple. The entry inside the main temple is open to Hindus only , others can have a visit around the temple area. If you are to visit the place, do check the opening hours in the newspaper as the place is open in limited hours only. Camera or photography is not allowed inside the main temple complex. Special pujas can be offered on payment of specified fee.\n\nA must visit place for Hindus devotees.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2019-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "876178B23D25D11C22BC59002928DAF1", "name": "Alok Mishra", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/aloknbsm", "username": "aloknbsm", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0d/70/ba/f3/aloknbsm.jpg", "contribution_count": 1202, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293890, "location_name": "Kathmandu", "location_name_detailed": "Kathmandu, Nepal"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-02-26", "published_at_date": "2019-02-26"}, {"review_id": 654861666, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r654861666-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "UNESCO World Heritage Site", "text": "The pagoda-style Hindu Pashupatinath Temple along the banks of the Bagmati river dates to 1696. It was named a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1979, and was not damaged in the 2015 earthquake. The Temple (really a complex of temples) is a sacred place of worship and serves as the seat of Nepal’s national deity, Lord Pashupatinath, the “Lord of the Animals”. You won’t be able to enter the Temple compound unless you are Hindu. But from the main gate you can catch a view of the backside of the statue of Nandi, Shiva’s bull. You can also view the back of the Temple from the east side of the Bagmati River. Here a series of ghats (steps) lead into the water, allowing ashes from the open-air cremations to be washed away by the river. As a westerner, I appreciated the opportunity to visit a place where centuries-old Hindu rituals are practiced. There is a unique spirit and energy here for the Hindu traditions of life, death and reincarnation.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2019-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "DF4D760647029B1DD8DE38B75FC501A0", "name": "Linda Y", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/994linday", "username": "994linday", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0f/05/8c/77/linda-y.jpg", "contribution_count": 5717, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 55870, "location_name": "Frisco", "location_name_detailed": "Frisco, Texas"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/16/97/0d/60/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/16/97/0d/7f/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/16/97/0d/9d/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/16/97/0f/05/pashupatinath-temple.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2019-02-26", "published_at_date": "2019-02-26"}, {"review_id": 654514112, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r654514112-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Like being in a National Geographic Episode!!", "text": "We arrived and paid the $10 (I don’t know how people can complain about the fee in one of the world’s poorest countries)\n\nWe took a guide (highly recommended) Thats cost us another $10. His knowledge was amazing and he took us via shortcuts to all the best photo spots and points of interest. \n\nWe watched the pagati arati that starts around 1840 from the opposite bank, all the the while families are cremating their dead on open pyres making for a truly fascinating look at life and death in contrast. No matter the caste or the wealth in life, all of these Hindus end up on a pyre on the same river bank. \n\nDon’t be put off by the monkeys.... they stay away from you and don’t be pushed into paying too much for photographs with the holy men/gurus, pay what you can afford but be wary that these donations are what they live off. \n\nOverall a fascinating and worthwhile experience. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2019-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "D39169BE71E72C10049BD7CB61667C3D", "name": "RWM4204", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/RWM4204", "username": "RWM4204", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e9/60/default-avatar-2020-64.jpg", "contribution_count": 81, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293997, "location_name": "Manama", "location_name_detailed": "Manama, Bahrain"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-02-24", "published_at_date": "2019-02-24"}, {"review_id": 654430797, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r654430797-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Happy to see good changes.", "text": "Nicer and cleaner. More organized and great spiritual ferling. Evrytime we come to kathmandu we make sure to visit this place.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2019-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "3A3B2E1097BF4053A946E99D418AE791", "name": "Aroma Fine Indian Cuisine", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/aromatoronto", "username": "aromatoronto", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/32/ba/b0/ee/caption.jpg", "contribution_count": 22, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 155019, "location_name": "Toronto", "location_name_detailed": "Toronto, Canada"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-02-24", "published_at_date": "2019-02-24"}, {"review_id": 654010295, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r654010295-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Sacred Place Worth to Visit", "text": "An eye-opener on the religious & sacred complex where you can witness the cremation in the open. \nOnly Hindus are allowed to enter the temple...but it is already a Majestic view just seeing the whole place from outside.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "0EDA00A548EFFD72F2C9DAE0F0F1017C", "name": "Nancy", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/crystall_moon", "username": "crystall_moon", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-s/02/dc/dc/72/crystall-moon.jpg", "contribution_count": 87, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 294265, "location_name": "Singapore", "location_name_detailed": "Singapore, Singapore"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-02-22", "published_at_date": "2019-02-22"}, {"review_id": 654006578, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r654006578-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A must see Hindu Temple, Where Lord Shiva have 4 faces", "text": "A must see Hindu Temple, Where Lord Shiva have 4 faces. Whereas other parts of the world that you can see Lord Shiva in the form of Linga. Only here in Pashupati Nath Temple Lord Shiva have 4 faces.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2019-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "4DBCEA45AFC257528EFAA964FD209E86", "name": "Road777126", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Road777126", "username": "Road777126", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/ef/32/default-avatar-2020-12.jpg", "contribution_count": 11, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-02-22", "published_at_date": "2019-02-22"}, {"review_id": 653855242, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r653855242-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Breathtaking experience ", "text": "We were Told about the activities going on at this site.  The locals use it for a public cremation ceremony.  Nothing can prepare you for the sights, smell a and activity. Totally foreign to Americans but OPENS YOUR EYES TO THE REST OF THE WORLD, ESPECIALLY NEPAL", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2019-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "25B26CD88434333C271222CF917EF754", "name": "M Richard M", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/mrichardm2016", "username": "mrichardm2016", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/08/eb/71/d0/mrichardm.jpg", "contribution_count": 1711, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293890, "location_name": "Kathmandu", "location_name_detailed": "Kathmandu, Nepal"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-02-21", "published_at_date": "2019-02-21"}, {"review_id": 653831171, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r653831171-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Pashupatinath Temple Kathmandu", "text": "The Lord Shiva Temple visit is must if you are visiting kathmandu The ultimate creator /controller of universe.The architecture of the temple is excellent .The special thing which I seen is that if the person after death is cremated there then he will will directly go to heaven. We have attended the evening aarti/puja which is worth watching.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2018-12-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "838E9489BF02D0824D74EE1000BF8CED", "name": "vsyadav65", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/vsyadav65", "username": "vsyadav65", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/09/11/a4/be/vsyadav65.jpg", "contribution_count": 114, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 304551, "location_name": "New Delhi", "location_name_detailed": "New Delhi, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-02-21", "published_at_date": "2019-02-21"}, {"review_id": 653657468, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r653657468-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "PashupatiNath Temple", "text": "One of the best places I have visited in Nepal. This place has some kind of spiritual powers that you will feel the moment you arrive there. Try to be there in the morning because there are many things to explore and to know about. Don't miss the River Aarti aka evening river prayer. You can't take pictures inside the temple however you can go on the other and take a picture from above and its the most stunning view you will ever have of any temple. Take a local bus or a tuk-tuk instead of taxi as its more reasonable and easy mode of transport.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "8D040F5F01D0584B909A3FD9CC113084", "name": "Dipen S", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/DipenS08", "username": "DipenS08", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/13/0b/e7/75/dipen-s.jpg", "contribution_count": 35, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 1532344, "location_name": "Navi Mumbai", "location_name_detailed": "Navi Mumbai, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-02-20", "published_at_date": "2019-02-20"}, {"review_id": 653383289, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r653383289-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Temple visit", "text": "We visited this temple along with the others on our temple tour. There many areas to walk around and while some areas are being reconstructed after the earthquake it was very interesting.     ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2019-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "460920A6837247D0218D3A20EA6187DE", "name": "Rogy52", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Rogy52", "username": "Rogy52", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/22/53/c6/a1/rogy52.jpg", "contribution_count": 62, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255108, "location_name": "Hamilton", "location_name_detailed": "Hamilton, New Zealand"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-02-19", "published_at_date": "2019-02-19"}, {"review_id": 653278151, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r653278151-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Truly Hindu but enlightening to all", "text": "Although only Hindus can enter the main temple, there is a lot to see and learn here. From the naughty monkeys to the cows and other animals, it's an enlightening place. The cremation of people is sobering. It makes you realise that the end may come at any time. The ground is vast and full of different things. I had a guide and he was knowledgeable and nice. He helped me to understand all the various activities.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2019-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "75F52258F86003E75B925E6820C0CFF6", "name": "AlexanderAdedeji", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/AlexanderAdedeji", "username": "AlexanderAdedeji", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/06/1b/f2/3e/alexadedeji.jpg", "contribution_count": 67, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 186338, "location_name": "London", "location_name_detailed": "London, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-02-18", "published_at_date": "2019-02-18"}, {"review_id": 653170713, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r653170713-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "best temple in all of Kathmandu", "text": "Pashupati Nath is a must see place in Kathmandu. It is the center of Hinduism and is always full of various lights, sound and smells. great place", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2019-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "CA8F3942682902D6632BBAC21044276E", "name": "David Smith", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/DaveTraveller69", "username": "DaveTraveller69", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e5/2b/default-avatar-2020-52.jpg", "contribution_count": 3, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-02-18", "published_at_date": "2019-02-18"}, {"review_id": 653120850, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r653120850-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Do not miss this!", "text": "This is where the funeral ceremonies take place. It is an experience you should not miss!\nVery somber, beautiful and educational in regard to learning the customs of other cultures", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2019-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "37A2ECBC4511515585076EFFC6B7ECFC", "name": "Hotshot47150", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/hotshot47150", "username": "hotshot47150", "avatar": null, "contribution_count": 28, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 37364, "location_name": "New Albany", "location_name_detailed": "New Albany, Indiana"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-02-18", "published_at_date": "2019-02-18"}, {"review_id": 652485191, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r652485191-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Amazing Arati in the evening", "text": "Had the opportunity to observe the magnificent evening Aarati at the Pashupatinath Temple. It was a great experience for me. I had never seen something like that in my life. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2019-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "3B4AC04A51FCD9FCF59DF2D6C1BFFBD4", "name": "Mason j", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/masonj359", "username": "masonj359", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f2/59/default-avatar-2020-24.jpg", "contribution_count": 1, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-02-15", "published_at_date": "2019-02-15"}, {"review_id": 652312374, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r652312374-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Good", "text": "Hindu temple, number of people coming from indiad, local people doing some of their ceremonies, not allow to enter inside the temple if you are not Hindu", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2019-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "7917B662A5C6BA45BE3D36FB3EC8CE0C", "name": "رائحة القهوة جغرافيا", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/sae3406", "username": "sae3406", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/09/53/7c/16/caption.jpg", "contribution_count": 58, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/16/76/33/7a/20190208-131719-largejpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/16/76/33/7b/20190208-130843-largejpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2019-02-14", "published_at_date": "2019-02-14"}, {"review_id": 652269060, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r652269060-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Didn't Enter, Only Friends Went in", "text": "One thing I can reviewed is the shops/market outside the temple. Most of them selling items for prayers. Love the colourful powder  where they usually use it for kolan. They were vibrant colours. The people are friendly and more than often, the younger males offer to give a tour inside the temple without being forceful (which is nice compared to other attractions).  \n\nMy friends went in to have a look but only a Hindu can enter the actual temple. One of my non-Hindu friend just went around the place and witnessed live cremation next to the river. PSA - Definitely not for the faint-hearted. \n\nFor t